# Paiziq Documentation Rules — STRICT

- Docs are numbered and have fixed roles. Do not create overlapping docs:
  - `docs/01_*` scope · `02_ARCHITECTURE.md` design · `03_BUILD_DEPLOY_PLAN.md`
    plan · `04_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` how-to · `05_PROGRESS_TRACKER.md` status
  - `CHANGELOG.md` per-change history · `README.md` landing page
- Every behavior change is documented **with its version** in
  `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog headings, ISO dates `YYYY-MM-DD`).
- The tracker (`05_PROGRESS_TRACKER.md`) must stay human-readable:
  status tables use ✅ / 🔄 / ⬜ and the verification log is append-only
  (`| date | version | gate | result |`).
- Keep code snippets in docs runnable against the current API — if a
  public signature changes, update every doc snippet that uses it and
  the docs site (`docs/site/`) in the same change.
- Shell examples always use `python3` / `pip3`.
- The docs site under `docs/site/` is generated from real SDK behavior;
  never document invented endpoints, params, or version numbers.
